  "description": "Accessibility scanner for running Android and iOS apps, with first-class .NET MAUI support. Wraps Apple's accessibility audit and Google's Accessibility Test Framework, can capture what TalkBack says on Android, maps findings to WCAG 2.2 and labels the standards they are relevant to (Section 508, EN 301 549 and others), can point findings at a likely line in your own project (--source), and writes JSON, HTML, Markdown ticket, CSV, PDF and draft Accessibility Conformance Report output. Automated checks find only some issues; manual testing is still required.",
